1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,910
(Shi Zhongyuan as Useless Contact)
This time on "The Truth",

3
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,230
we actually played two roles.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,710
One was a stall owner in Ghost Market,

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,870
and the other was the head of security,

6
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,030
Helpful Contact.

7
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:14,820
Anything fun from this shoot
that you can share?

8
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,030
This time I got to wear normal clothes

9
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:22,110
and interact with the cast.

10
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,590
That was really fun.

11
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,470
They were all busy

12
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:26,830
looking for clues

13
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,190
in this super tense situation,

14
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:31,030
and since I knew
a little bit more than they did,

15
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,990
it was pretty entertaining to watch.

16
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,510
Especially when they came in,

17
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:35,470
I just said,

18
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,790
"Bring them all in."

19
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,390
And they came in so fast.

20
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,430
That cracked me up.

21
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,990
Because before that,
I'd been stressing over

22
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,710
how I was gonna get them inside.

23
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:49,030
One role was more historical,

24
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:49,790
and the other was modern.

25
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:51,090
Which one did you like more?

26
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,070
I liked both.

27
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:56,070
The historical one

28
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:58,870
had a bit more feel to it.

29
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,390
And usually

30
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,030
our themes are

31
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,470
a little creepy

32
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,190
or old-fashioned.

33
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,750
But in this episode,

34
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,910
I finally got to live my dream

35
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,710
(Dream come true)
of wearing a suit.

36
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:16,560
What was it like
playing a gangster again?

37
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,230
I have to talk about it.

38
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:21,710
I remember coming on last season,

39
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:23,990
and the role was
kinda gangster-like too.

40
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,430
(The Truth 3 EP03)
But I was wearing a security uniform.

41
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,550
This time, it felt like I'd levelled up.

42
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,270
It feels like I'm growing
with every season.

43
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,710
The water-gun battle today

44
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,750
was pretty intense too.

45
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,180
Who was the MVP tank for you?

46
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:38,870
The whole thing was so chaotic.

47
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,590
Everyone had shields up,

48
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,950
and then they started

49
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,830
spraying at us.

50
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:46,310
I honestly can't even
remember who was who.

51
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,190
I was seeing water everywhere.

52
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,270
But those in the front row

53
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,830
were definitely taking one for the team.

54
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,950
What stood out to you
most during filming?

55
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,070
Some of the cast

56
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,910
looked like they were injured,

57
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,670
but they were still doing

58
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,030
some pretty difficult moves.

59
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,790
I really respected that.

60
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:10,360
What kind of new role or gameplay

61
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,920
would you like to try next time?

62
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:16,470
I wanna try every costume possible.

63
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:17,030
I sound like

64
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,830
(Trying every look)
I'm collecting stamps.

65
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,150
I just want to collect them all.

66
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,630
I've done historical costumes,

67
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,790
a suit,

68
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,110
and the security uniform.

69
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,070
So now I'm curious

70
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,310
what look I'll get next.

71
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,550
Use one sentence to recommend
"The Truth 4" to our audience.

72
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,510
(Full approval)
Tense, exciting, and fun.

73
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:36,220
What was it like bidding
against the players

74
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:38,200
(Lin Tan as An Yi)
for the item?

75
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:39,950
I was really excited.

76
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,790
I'd never been

77
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,870
to a real auction before,

78
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,790
so I finally got to experience one.

79
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,830
Every time I raised my paddle

80
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:48,190
was so fun and exciting.

81
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,540
Which player stood out to you most?

82
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:52,950
During the auction,

83
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,590
Ding Chengxin stood out the most.

84
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,550
He was the loudest,

85
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,430
and he even stood up.

86
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:59,310
It turned into this
funny standoff with us.

87
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,030
I had a lot of fun.

88
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:02,760
Did anything funny
happen during filming?

89
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,510
I honestly didn't expect

90
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,990
them to be that into the auction.

91
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,190
(So into it)
They were fully immersed.

92
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,390
And once they got into it,

93
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,550
we got into it too.

94
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,470
That back-and-forth

95
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,590
made it really fun.

96
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,630
I'll never forget it.

97
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:16,190
In one sentence, recommend "The Truth 4"

98
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:16,890
to our audience.

99
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,630
That auction wore me out.

100
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:19,510
Come watch it.

101
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,530
(Fu Jiahua as Fu Hao)
You've been on "The Truth 4" a lot.

102
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:23,990
Have you noticed
any changes in the players?

103
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,230
They keep looking better.

104
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,430
Once they're all together,

105
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:29,230
everyone has their own role to play,

106
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:31,510
and they all handle

107
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,910
their part really well.

108
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,550
That's what makes a team.

109
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,750
Like Jin Jing,

110
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,830
she's really good at talking

111
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,790
with us NPCs.

112
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,030
And Liu Yuning too.

113
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:48,590
For example, if he asks us something

114
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,070
we're not allowed to answer,

115
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:50,910
he'll look at our reactions

116
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:51,830
and immediately

117
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,430
realize

118
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,510
"Okay, they can't talk about this".

119
00:03:53,770 --> 00:03:54,100
Yeah.

120
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,950
And everyone else too.

121
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:56,990
They're all really fun.

122
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:59,270
You've played a security guard
and a boss this season.

123
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:01,200
What kind of role
would you like to try next?

124
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,790
I don't even know
what my style is anymore.

125
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,750
Maybe in the players' eyes,

126
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:09,510
I'm basically the villain now.

127
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:13,430
Like that guide I played
a few episodes ago,

128
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,660
with my black hat,

129
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,590
black veil,

130
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,950
and heavy makeup.

131
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,070
The second I showed up
and said my first line,

132
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,150
the players went, "New captain."

133
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,790
At that point,
there was nothing I could do.

134
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,750
So maybe I'll just keep

135
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,910
being a villain.

136
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:30,580
Any funny moments when filming

137
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,610
with the other NPCs?

138
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,230
A lot.

139
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:37,590
This time, with everyone
from the Ghost Market,

140
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,070
we tested out

141
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:42,630
the game mechanics ourselves.

142
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,390
We'd get some friends

143
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,670
to try it together.

144
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,670
It was pretty fun.

145
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:51,510
And none of the Ghost Market NPCs

146
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,030
were really

147
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,590
gamers before.

148
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,510
But once they got the game rules,

149
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,030
they started finding people
to play with every day.

150
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,550
Maybe they wanted
to make some extra cash,

151
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,470
or maybe they just wanted to play.

152
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,750
Maybe they just enjoyed it.

153
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:07,480
Which player stood out
to you most this time?

154
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,410
Can you give an example?

155
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,180
Zhang Linghe.

156
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:12,470
Definitely Zhang Linghe.

157
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,910
Because he recognized me immediately.

158
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,190
(The Truth EP04's Captain) He knew I was
the new captain from a few episodes ago.

159
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:19,230
He kept asking me,

160
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,910
"What are you doing here?"

161
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,830
"What are you doing here?"

162
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,230
"You're a scammer."

163
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:25,960
(Made quite an impression)

164
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:26,430
"What are you doing here?"

165
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:26,960
Yeah, it's him.

166
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,350
He just kept questioning me.

167
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,150
And I wanted to talk to him,

168
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:30,950
but because of my character,

169
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,230
I couldn't really say much.

170
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:32,720
Yeah.

171
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,870
Still, I was really happy.

172
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:36,510
If the players remembered my character,

173
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,390
then I guess

174
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,430
I left an impression on them.

175
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,390
That made me really happy.

176
00:05:40,390 --> 00:05:40,600
Yeah.

177
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:43,380
If you had to rank
the players' reasoning skills,

178
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,700
(Sui Xin as Helpful Contact)
who would rank first?

179
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,870
Liu Yuning, without a doubt.

180
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,910
Because in that last part,

181
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,950
the second he walked in,

182
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,350
he basically said aloud

183
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:57,070
every single clue

184
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,430
and piece of information

185
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:01,670
I wanted to give them.

186
00:06:02,590 --> 00:06:05,370
Anything especially funny
or memorable during filming?

187
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,310
For me, the best part today

188
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:08,790
was still Liu Yuning.

189
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:09,830
We're heading downstairs later.

190
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,670
I think he's a genius.

191
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,710
When it comes to deduction,

192
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,590
his logic is incredibly clear.

193
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,870
He can still remember information

194
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,070
from way earlier in the timeline.

195
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:22,350
He can connect

196
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,510
everything together,

197
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,830
and keep the story moving.

198
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,320
This is your first time playing
an NPC on a variety show.

199
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:31,240
How is it different
from performing in live theatre?

200
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:32,910
(Immersive theatre "Inside No. 9", Victor)
It's different.

201
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:38,110
It's different from both stage
and screen acting.

202
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,230
Because everything unfolds continuously,

203
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,430
and as the character,

204
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,350
we just complete our role

205
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:45,630
and do whatever the situation requires.

206
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:49,470
(Guiding players toward clues)
Here, we must guide players

207
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,270
toward discovering clues themselves.
That's our job.

208
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:55,590
Then they have to think,

209
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,230
discuss,

210
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,670
reason things out,

211
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:00,510
and find the clue themselves.

212
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,870
Once they find it,

213
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:02,790
we pick things up from there

214
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:04,030
and move on

215
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,390
to the next part.

216
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:05,710
So yeah,

217
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,510
it's pretty different
from normal acting.

218
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:08,270
But it's really fun.

219
00:07:08,650 --> 00:07:09,930
If you get the chance,

220
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,310
would you like to play
more variety-show NPCs?

221
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,390
Of course.

222
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:16,790
I think this kind of NPC performance

223
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:17,990
is really interesting.

224
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,190
For an actor,

225
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,230
it's also great training.

226
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,270
Even after you finish

227
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,030
guiding them

228
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:25,270
and they start discussing,

229
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,830
you still have to keep watching them.

230
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:27,550
You need to know

231
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,230
how far they've gotten,

232
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:29,950
what stage they're at,

233
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:31,070
when to step in,

234
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,990
and when to move things along.

235
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,910
That's great practice for an actor too.

236
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:37,190
This whole theme,

237
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,550
including the Longdong Army from before
and the Helpful Contact

238
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,070
are heroic roles.

239
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:43,260
If you could choose, would you
keep playing good guys

240
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,540
or try something different?

241
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,590
This is my first time

242
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,550
playing an NPC.

243
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,510
About 95% of my stage roles

244
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,230
are villains.

245
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:58,950
So I'm really thankful

246
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,110
they gave me two

247
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:05,190
very positive roles here.

248
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,390
If I get another chance

249
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,990
to play an NPC on a variety show,

250
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,550
I'm good with anything.

251
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:15,790
I felt pretty comfortable
in these two roles too.

252
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,070
For once, I don't have to be onstage

253
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:22,110
playing villains
or getting caught up in romance.

254
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,510
Playing someone

255
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:25,190
more positive and uplifting

256
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,430
is nice.

257
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,390
So next time, I'm open to anything.

258
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:28,990
As long as I get the chance,

259
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:29,950
I'm happy.

260
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,750
If you had one sentence to recommend "The Truth 4",

261
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:33,600
what would you say?

262
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:36,310
I've filmed about two episodes now,

263
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,310
and honestly,

264
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:39,190
there's a lot worth watching.

265
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,990
First, the production team
really puts in the work.

266
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,510
From the NPC makeup and costumes

267
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:47,310
to all the character settings

268
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,870
- and the story logic too.
- Sold! Congrats, Mr. Fu.

269
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,230
The mystery and reasoning

270
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,230
are both done

271
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:56,390
to a very high standard.

272
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,990
So I hope everyone checks it out.

273
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:58,670
Thank you.

274
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:01,430
=The Truth=

275
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:02,780
(SVIP: New episodes
every Wed & Thu at 12PM)

276
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:03,940
(VIP: Available the next day at 12PM,
with one week early access)
